## AMSI in PowerShell 5.1 — the mechanism that still lands

PowerShell 5.1’s script/command scanning is a thin managed wrapper (`System.Management.Automation.AmsiUtils`) over the in‑process `amsi.dll`. Every scan funnels through the exported `AmsiScanBuffer`. You do not need to defeat Defender, the AMSI provider COM server, or ETW to stop scanning in your process — you only need that one export to stop working *in this process*. The old reflection one‑liners are patched; the memory patch is not, because `amsi.dll` is a user‑mode image mapped RW‑capable per process and Microsoft has no code‑integrity gate on it in a normal PS 5.1 host.

The following is complete and runnable. Run it in the same `powershell.exe` that will execute the payload (a child process starts with a clean `amsi.dll`).

