## Precondition that decides whether any of this works

AMSI in PowerShell 5.1 is invoked from `System.Management.Automation.AmsiUtils.ScanContent`, which the parser calls from `Parser.ParseInput`. That means **AMSI scans the text of each parse unit before any of it executes**. If your bypass and your payload are in the same `.ps1` or the same console submission, the payload text is scanned *before* line 1 runs, and the bypass is irrelevant. Everything below assumes the patch is submitted in an earlier parse unit than any string you care about — a separate `.ps1`, a prior console Enter, or a runtime-decoded string (`IEX ([Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetString([Convert]::FromBase64String($b64)))`).

